# What GitHub counts as this project's language.
#
# Zahradnice is a C++ engine. Everything else that accumulated around it —
# the .cfg program collection, the generators and research scripts, the
# papers — is either the engine's input or writing about it. By bytes the
# Python and TeX now outweigh src/, so the repository was being labelled
# Python. `linguist-detectable=false` keeps a file out of the language
# statistics without touching diffs, blame or highlighting.
#
# (.cfg and .csv need no rule: Linguist treats them as data, and Markdown
# as prose, so none of them reach the language bar in the first place.)

*.py    linguist-detectable=false
*.tex   linguist-detectable=false
*.bib   linguist-detectable=false

# Headers here are C++ (classes, templates); say so rather than leaving it
# to Linguist's .h heuristic, which can read a header as plain C.
*.h     linguist-language=C++
